# s3-04 -> CORE-WIRE-G2

## native/core/crates/mixdog-tools/src/desktop/mod.rs, `mod computer_image_output;` after `mod computer_gnome;`, and `mod computer_marks_draw;` after `pub mod computer_linux;`
(`pub mod` instead of `mod` for either when the compose call below sits outside mixdog-tools; the items are `ImageOutput` and `paint_marks`, `paint_marks_or_input`, `Mark`, `MarkSource`, `PaintedImage`, `Overlay`, `PaintError`.)

## native/core/Cargo.toml
No new workspace dependency: `flate2` and `jpeg-decoder` are already in `[workspace.dependencies]` and in Cargo.lock (g25-fu-cu-c replaced `png` and `jpeg-encoder`, which the offline lock does not have). Only the edge below; `cargo hakari generate` after it.

## native/core/crates/mixdog-tools/Cargo.toml `[dependencies]`
    flate2 = { workspace = true }
    jpeg-decoder = { workspace = true }

## JPEG burn-in (open)
PNG frames are burned in and re-encoded with flate2. A JPEG frame is decoded but cannot be re-encoded: `jpeg-encoder` 0.6 (and nothing else in the lock) would do it. It must be fetched into the registry cache and added to Cargo.lock; then `encode()` in computer_marks_draw.rs takes the one-line jpeg_encoder::Encoder call. Until then a JPEG frame is returned unmarked with `overlay_error` set to the reason.

## compose call
None here: the two modules are used by the capture reply, which is s3-03's/s3-17's wiring of the SOM mode and `image_output: "file"`:
- `ImageOutput::new(config.data_dir)` once per backend, `write(session_id, frame_id, bytes, mime)` -> on Err keep the image inline (as persistCaptureImage).
- `paint_marks_or_input(...)` for `mode == "som"` with the elements' `mark`/`bounds`/`source`; `rendered` / `error` feed `overlay_rendered` / `overlay_error`.
No SERVICE_PENDING name is touched by this task.
